SARS-CoV-2 Seasonality Manuscript Analyses Overview

This R script contains the full analysis pipeline for the manuscript: "Interplay of Immunity, Climate, and Viral Evolution Explains
Semiannual SARS-CoV-2 Dynamics with Implications for Control". It implements a compartmental mechanistic two-tier SEIRS-V model
(Susceptible–Exposed–Infectious–Recovered–Vaccinated) ODE system with 10 compartments (S, E, I, R, V for each of two immunity tiers) 
and models hospitalization time series ten US states (GA, MI, MN, NY, OH, TN, CA, CO, OR, UT) and generates all manuscript 
figures. Parameter estimates are fixed from the literature or fitted in prior model calibration procedures. 

Files: 
- Run_COVID_Seasonality_Analyses: Code to generate each analyses and figures in main text.
- Run_COVID_Seasonality_Supplementary: Code to generate all analyses and figures in the supplementary.

Data
- All data used to run this code is found in data/processed folder. 
